    "findings": [
      "Observed root cause: Shell::report renders diagnostics via mori_diagnostics::render::render_colored with miette::GraphicalReportHandler::new_themed(GraphicalTheme::unicode()) capped at 80 columns (WIDTH), inserting leading indentation and a single Unicode '\u2502' (U+2502) continuation gutter at the start of wrapped continuation lines.",
      "In the first test execution (commit c24bfc005910972663954eecfaf6d99698064438, tree 7a89671b88b8e9e879c24657a299adcf6b7fac1e), normalize_ws only called split_whitespace().join(\" \"), leaving the continuation gutter token '\u2502' inside normalized stderr ('...has no Midnight \u2502 support...' and '...requires --target \u2502 and --at together').",
      "Updated normalize_ws in native_feature_boundary.rs to iterate non-empty trimmed lines, preserve the first non-empty line intact, strip at most one leading '\u2502' continuation gutter from subsequent continuation lines, and join whitespace tokens with single spaces while preserving any internal '\u2502' characters in semantic payload.",
      "Added two pure literal assertions at the start of native_routes_report_unavailable_before_io verifying wrapped continuation gutter removal (with leading newline) and preservation of internal/subsequent '\u2502' tokens without changing the 27 catalog cases, 44 planned subprocess invocations, expected messages, exit codes, or filesystem sentinel checks."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Author-only source patch turn: no cargo build, test execution, or subprocess calls were performed in this turn.",
      "The recorded cold test run (exitCode 101) panicked on the first failing assertion in each of the 2 test functions and therefore did not complete all 44 planned mori child invocations; fresh non-author review and a new concrete test execution attempt are required before claiming runtime pass."
    ],
    "reviewToken": "doctorwatson-native-availability-gutter-source-author-20261018-a1-whole-source-patch",
    "sourcePatch": "--- a/native_feature_boundary.rs\n+++ b/native_feature_boundary.rs\n@@ -74,7 +74,24 @@\n }\n \n fn normalize_ws(text: &str) -> String {\n-    text.split_whitespace().collect::<Vec<_>>().join(\" \")\n+    let mut seen_line = false;\n+    text.lines()\n+        .filter_map(|line| {\n+            let trimmed = line.trim_start();\n+            if trimmed.is_empty() {\n+                return None;\n+            }\n+            let content = if seen_line {\n+                trimmed.strip_prefix('\u2502').unwrap_or(trimmed)\n+            } else {\n+                seen_line = true;\n+                trimmed\n+            };\n+            Some(content)\n+        })\n+        .flat_map(str::split_whitespace)\n+        .collect::<Vec<_>>()\n+        .join(\" \")\n }\n \n fn run_mori(cwd: &Path, args: &[&str]) -> (Option<i32>, Vec<u8>, String) {\n@@ -142,6 +159,17 @@\n \n #[test]\n fn native_routes_report_unavailable_before_io() {\n+    assert_eq!(\n+        normalize_ws(\n+            \"\\n  \u00d7 mori::command::native-unavailable: This mori build has no Midnight\\n  \u2502 support. Rebuild with the native feature enabled.\\n\"\n+        ),\n+        format!(\"\u00d7 {NATIVE_CODE}: {NATIVE_MSG}\")\n+    );\n+    assert_eq!(\n+        normalize_ws(\"  \u00d7 header \u2502 keep\\n    \u2502 \u2502 body \u2502 keep\\n\"),\n+        \"\u00d7 header \u2502 keep \u2502 body \u2502 keep\"\n+    );\n+\n     let routes: Vec<(&str, Vec<&str>)> = vec![\n         (\n             \"compile\",\n",
    "summary": "Repaired normalize_ws in native_feature_boundary.rs to strip leading indentation and at most one leading Unicode '\u2502' miette continuation gutter on continuation lines before whitespace normalization, preserving internal '\u2502' payload characters and all 27 catalog cases / 44 planned invocations unchanged.",
    "toolAction": "Finishing gutter normalization repair patch",
    "toolSummary": "Finish gutter normalization source patch"
